      "external_key": "q-precalculus-functions-inverse-functions",
      "topic": "Functions",
      "subtopic": "Inverse functions",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x) = {{coef(a,'x')}} {{signed(b)}}$.",
      "answer": "$f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{ x {{signed(-b)}} }{ {{a}} }$",
      "solution": "Write $y = {{coef(a,'x')}} {{signed(b)}}$, swap $x$ and $y$, then solve: $x {{signed(-b)}} = {{coef(a,'y')}}$, so $y = \\dfrac{ x {{signed(-b)}} }{ {{a}} }$.",
