      "external_key": "q-precalculus-trigonometry-law-of-sines",
      "topic": "Trigonometry",
      "subtopic": "Law of sines",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "In triangle $ABC$, $\\angle A = {{a}}^\\circ$, $\\angle B = {{b}}^\\circ$, and side $a = {{s}}$. Find side $b$ to two decimal places.",
      "answer": "${{fmt(s * sin(b * pi / 180) / sin(a * pi / 180), 2)}}$",
      "solution": "By the law of sines $\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A} = \\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}$, so $b = \\dfrac{ {{s}} \\sin({{b}}^\\circ) }{ \\sin({{a}}^\\circ) } = {{fmt(s * sin(b * pi / 180) / sin(a * pi / 180), 2)}}$.",
