      "topic": "Rational Functions",
      "subtopic": "Vertical asymptotes and holes",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "Identify any holes and vertical asymptotes of $f(x) = \\dfrac{ x^2 {{term(-(p + q),'x')}} {{signed(p*q)}} }{ x {{signed(-p)}} }$.",
      "answer": "A hole at $x = {{p}}$; no vertical asymptote.",
      "solution": "The numerator factors as $(x {{signed(-p)}})(x {{signed(-q)}})$, so the factor $x {{signed(-p)}}$ cancels. A cancelling factor leaves a hole rather than an asymptote, so there is a hole at $x = {{p}}$ and nothing else.",
