      "external_key": "q-precalculus-conic-sections-circles",
      "topic": "Conic Sections",
      "subtopic": "Circles",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "Find the centre and radius of the circle $x^2 {{term(-2*h,'x')}} + y^2 {{term(-2*k,'y')}} {{signed(h*h + k*k - r*r)}} = 0$.",
      "answer": "Centre $({{h}}, {{k}})$, radius ${{r}}$.",
      "solution": "Complete the square in $x$ and in $y$: $(x {{signed(-h)}})^2 + (y {{signed(-k)}})^2 = {{r*r}}$. That is the standard form, so the centre is $({{h}}, {{k}})$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{ {{r*r}} } = {{r}}$.",
